a class template specialization is spelled without the namespace it was declared in: cxx1 writes ?most@?$Bounds@H@@SAHXZ where cl writes ?most@?$Bounds@H@lim@@SAHXZ. Templates are keyed by their bare name here, so a specialization does not know which namespace it came from - docs/CONFORMANCE.md records that and what fixing it costs, and template-id-qualified-and-deduced.nonames records the same difference against clang. What this case is about, a namespace-qualified template-id as a qualifier and a deduced member template, is checked by run-cases.cmd on the box and run.sh on the other two.
